===Adjective===
{{en-adj|more}}

# Point-like; consisting of or marked with one or more points.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1918|author=Franklin Henry Martin|title=Surgery, Gynecology & Obstetrics|page=11
|text={{...}} with a punctuate wound of entrance and a small wound of exit, may very properly be treated with a dry dressing and not disturbed, and in a large proportion of the cases there will be little or no tissue reaction that will require{{nb...}}}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1922|title=Medical Review of Reviews|page=315
|text={{...}} with a punctuate eruption on the hard palate, and a peppery red punctuate rash becoming generalized within twenty-four hours can mean nothing else but scarlet fever. Add to this the circumoral pallor and the glandular enlargements{{nb...}}}}
#* {{quote-book|en|date=2005-03-22|author=Tor Savidge|author2=Charalabos Pothulakis|title=Microbial Imaging|publisher=Elsevier|isbn=9780125215350|page=16
|text=Positive HPV 16 hybridization signal in two cervical carcinomas. A '''punctuate''' signal (a) and a '''punctuate''' and diffuse signal (b).}}
#* {{quote-book|en|date=2012-01-25|author=Ming Zhou|author2=George Netto|author3=Jonathan I Epstein|title=Uropathology E-Book: A Volume in the High Yield Pathology Series|publisher=Elsevier Health Sciences|isbn=9781455737840|page=403
|text={{...}} with a '''punctuate''' or “salt and pepper” chromatin pattern • Associated with focal epidermoid cyst or teratoma in 25% of cases • Lacks intratubular germ cell neoplasia Immunopathology (including immunohistochemistry){{nb...}}}}
#* {{quote-book|en|date=2012-11-08|author=Zoran Rumboldt|author2=Mauricio Castillo|author3=Benjamin Huang|title=Brain Imaging with MRI and CT: An Image Pattern Approach|publisher=Cambridge University Press|isbn=9780521119443|page=344
|text={{...}} with a '''punctuate''' wall calcification (arrow) along the right postcentral sulcus.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|date=2019-04-13|author=Beatrice Morio|author2=Luc Penicaud|author3=Michel Rigoulet|title=Mitochondria in Obesity and Type 2 Diabetes: Comprehensive Review on Mitochondrial Functioning and Involvement in Metabolic Diseases|publisher=Academic Press|isbn=9780128118597|page=255
|text={{...}} looking more '''punctuate'''. This mechanism is accompanied by a transient increase of mROS that could be inhibited by decreasing DRP1, thus decreasing DRP1/FIS1 association, and thus fission. In fasting animals, hypothalamic mitochondria appear{{nb...}}}}

